From 423c942dd307116985537293b96954bd3741da87 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: starbite <starbite@local>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 19:05:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] patch: 0323-sweet-hid-ios26-digitizer.patch

Touch for iOS 26: IOHIDFamily-2238 changed IOHIDDigitizerEventData from
16.16 IOFixed members (0x68 bytes, the 1915 layout SweetHID was built
from) to IOHIDDouble (0xa0, layout from the macOS 26.5 KDK's
IOHIDFamily.kext DWARF). iOS 26 parsed our bytes with the new layout:
positions were garbage and the rest landed in generationCount and the
update masks, so backboardd's BKDigitizer dropped every touch ("got an
event update with generation:3 but I can't find any pending items").
The double members are stored as IEEE-754 bits converted from fixed with
integer arithmetic (no FP in the kernel); field macros and the digitizer
constructors go through sweet_fixed_to_dbits / sweet_dbits_to_fixed.
- starlte_touch.c: sweetswipe=3 = Home to unlock, then taps and a page swipe on the iOS 26 home screen
- SweetHID.cpp: digitizer collection and contacts carry IsDisplayIntegrated (iOS 26 touch streams filter detached touches)
- IOHIDEvent.cpp (0323): iOS 26 event serialization, a queue-element header per event and child depth (IOHIDFamily-2238), so digitizer children reach userland
